  "lesson": "# Cosine similarity matrix\n\nGiven `X` of shape `(n, d)`, return the `(n, n)` matrix whose `[i, j]` entry is the cosine of the angle between rows `i` and `j`. A zero row has no direction: define its similarity with everything as 0 (not NaN).\n\n**Interview signal:** normalise the rows once, then a single matmul (this is the core of embedding search). Normalising *columns* is the classic axis slip.\n",
  "spec": "\"\"\"Starter file shown to the player.\"\"\"\nimport numpy as np\n\n\ndef cosine_sim(X):\n    \"\"\"Return the (n, n) matrix of cosine similarities between rows of X (zero rows give similarity 0).\"\"\"\n    raise NotImplementedError\n",
  "visibleTests": "import numpy as np\nfrom nc_test import assert_close, python_lines\n\n\ndef test_orthogonal_and_parallel():\n    S = cosine_sim([[1.0, 0.0], [0.0, 2.0], [3.0, 0.0]])\n    assert_close(S, [[1, 0, 1], [0, 1, 0], [1, 0, 1]])\n\n\ndef test_opposite():\n    assert_close(cosine_sim([[1.0, 1.0], [-2.0, -2.0]])[0, 1], -1.0)\n\ndef _vectorised(fn, *args, limit=40):\n    out, lines = python_lines(fn, *args)\n    assert lines <= limit, f\"{lines} Python lines executed: the work is happening in a Python loop, not in numpy\"\n    return out\n",
  "hiddenTests": "import numpy as np\nfrom nc_test import assert_close, python_lines\n\n\ndef test_hidden_matches_pairwise_formula():\n    X = np.random.default_rng(9).normal(size=(8, 5))\n    ref = np.array([[a @ b / (np.linalg.norm(a) * np.linalg.norm(b)) for b in X] for a in X])\n    assert_close(cosine_sim(X), ref)\n\n\ndef test_hidden_zero_row_gives_zero_not_nan():\n    S = cosine_sim([[0.0, 0.0], [1.0, 2.0]])\n    assert np.isfinite(S).all(), \"zero row divided by zero\"\n    assert_close(S[0], [0.0, 0.0])\n    assert_close(S[1, 1], 1.0)\n\n\ndef test_hidden_symmetric_with_unit_diagonal():\n    X = np.random.default_rng(10).normal(size=(6, 3))\n    S = cosine_sim(X)\n    assert_close(S, S.T)\n    assert_close(np.diag(S), np.ones(6))\n\n\ndef test_hidden_scale_invariant():\n    X = np.random.default_rng(11).normal(size=(5, 4))\n    assert_close(cosine_sim(X), cosine_sim(X * np.array([[1], [10], [0.1], [5], [100]])))\n\n\ndef test_hidden_no_python_loop():\n    X = np.random.default_rng(12).normal(size=(400, 32))\n    assert _vectorised(cosine_sim, X).shape == (400, 400)\n\ndef _vectorised(fn, *args, limit=40):\n    out, lines = python_lines(fn, *args)\n    assert lines <= limit, f\"{lines} Python lines executed: the work is happening in a Python loop, not in numpy\"\n    return out\n"
