  "lesson": "# One-hot encoding\n\nTurn integer class `labels` (length n, values in `0..k-1`) into an `(n, k)` float matrix with a single 1 per row. `k` is given: a batch may not contain every class, so never infer it from `labels.max()`.\n\nRaise `ValueError` for a label outside `0..k-1` (negative indices would silently wrap in numpy).\n\n**Interview signal:** fancy indexing `out[np.arange(n), labels] = 1`, and guarding the silent-wrap trap.\n",
  "spec": "\"\"\"Starter file shown to the player.\"\"\"\nimport numpy as np\n\n\ndef one_hot(labels, k):\n    \"\"\"Return an (n, k) float array with a 1 at [i, labels[i]]. No Python loops.\"\"\"\n    raise NotImplementedError\n",
  "visibleTests": "import numpy as np\nfrom nc_test import assert_close, python_lines\n\n\ndef test_basic():\n    assert_close(one_hot([0, 2, 1], 3), [[1, 0, 0], [0, 0, 1], [0, 1, 0]])\n\n\ndef test_empty():\n    assert one_hot([], 4).shape == (0, 4)\n\ndef _vectorised(fn, *args, limit=40):\n    out, lines = python_lines(fn, *args)\n    assert lines <= limit, f\"{lines} Python lines executed: the work is happening in a Python loop, not in numpy\"\n    return out\n",
  "hiddenTests": "import numpy as np\nfrom nc_test import assert_close, python_lines\n\n\ndef test_hidden_missing_classes_keep_width():\n    out = one_hot([1, 1], 5)\n    assert out.shape == (2, 5)\n    assert_close(out.sum(axis=0), [0, 2, 0, 0, 0])\n\n\ndef test_hidden_out_of_range_raises():\n    for bad in ([3], [-1], [0, 5]):\n        try:\n            one_hot(bad, 3)\n        except ValueError:\n            continue\n        raise AssertionError(f\"{bad} should raise ValueError (a negative label would silently wrap)\")\n\n\ndef test_hidden_dtype_is_float_and_rows_sum_to_one():\n    out = one_hot(np.array([4, 0, 0, 3]), 5)\n    assert out.dtype.kind == \"f\"\n    assert_close(out.sum(axis=1), np.ones(4))\n\n\ndef test_hidden_matches_identity_rows():\n    labels = np.random.default_rng(7).integers(0, 6, size=40)\n    assert_close(one_hot(labels, 6), np.eye(6)[labels])\n\n\ndef test_hidden_no_python_loop():\n    labels = np.random.default_rng(8).integers(0, 10, size=5000)\n    assert _vectorised(one_hot, labels, 10).shape == (5000, 10)\n\ndef _vectorised(fn, *args, limit=40):\n    out, lines = python_lines(fn, *args)\n    assert lines <= limit, f\"{lines} Python lines executed: the work is happening in a Python loop, not in numpy\"\n    return out\n"
